// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
// kernel/user/traypop.fi -- THE TRAY FLYOUT OF THE BAR (W-TRAY2, 12.10.2026).
//
// One scene window of the bar's scene host (window 6, like barpop / taskview; NOT code in
// taskbar.fi, which sits at its size limit). It is opened by the tray chevron when the tray has
// icons in the overflow, and shows three things, top down:
//
//   network     a VECTOR glyph of the real state + the sentence the bar's tooltip uses
//   sound       speaker glyph, mute button and a volume slider (SYS_AUDGET / SYS_AUDSET: the same
//               calls as the quick settings; "no audio device" when the kernel has none)
//   microphone  glyph + "in use by N programs" / "muted" + mute button -- real numbers (SYS_AUDGET A_CAPUSERS/A_CAPMUTE)
//   overflow    one row per item of lib/fui/tray.fi (PLACE_OVERFLOW): glyph, name, a "..." button
//               that opens the item's context menu (its entries + "Move up" + "Hide")
//
// GLYPHS are vectors (strokes + rounded plates through fUi's painter), no emoji, no icon font:
//   ethernet  online / limited (no address) / no route ("!" badge) / no carrier (slash)
//   wlan      bars 0..4 -- drawn only when `net_kind()` says Wi-Fi; there is NO Wi-Fi driver (roadmap
//             N-005), so the kind is always Ethernet today and these bars never appear
//   speaker   off / 1 / 2 waves, muted (cross)      mic   plain / muted (slash)      chevron
// There is no airplane mode in this system, so there is no airplane glyph (a symbol for a switch
// that does not exist would be a lie).
//
// WHERE THE ITEMS COME FROM. The action-bus message names for tray registration are not defined
// yet (docs/TRAY.md). Until they are, programs register by writing /etc/tray.items, one item per
// line:  owner|icon|tooltip     (icon = number; 1 net, 2 sound, 3 mic are the system glyphs, any
// other number draws the first letter of the owner on a plate). The flyout reads it when it opens
// and adds owners it does not know yet. Two more line kinds are test aids:
//   mic|<users>|<muted>   the STUB capture source: there is no capture path in the kernel (no
//                         SYS_AUDREAD, roadmap), so the mic indicator can only show what this line says
//   sheet                 adds a glyph sheet (every state of every glyph) under the items
//
// Serial lines (read by tools/traypop/run.sh):
//   traypop: open n=<overflow items> x= y= w= h=
//   traypop: item <i> id= owner= tip=
//   traypop: click id= owner=          traypop: menu id=        traypop: pick id= action=
//   traypop: vol <0..100> rc=          traypop: mute <0|1>      traypop: shut <why>

profile kernel

